Z||000000||icee||06-25-2001||05:17 PM||||hi. Recently i met a guy selling an 87 fiero gt. i think it has 30k miles on it. it looks really good new paint, new tires(low profiel) new exaust manifolds. and hes replaced a lot of other stuff he said he had intended on keeping the car but came across a corvet that he couldnt passup and its true he did hes pretty well known in the town. He also owns a mecanic shop. and told me if i bought it and had any probemls to bring it in and he has a parts fiero and can fix it up cheap. Im not sure what to do... hes asking 4,ooo for it. and i cant afford to get something that ganna break down. Im leaving for college at the end of the summer. Ive heard from many people fieros break down all the time and are very expensive to work on... the only thing i saw wrong with the car is the scoop thing on the side of the car is missing...<P>help help help. i feel like i might be passing up a good deal.. i think the car looks pretty good.||||reg||9
Z||000001||icee||06-25-2001||05:20 PM||||also does anyone know if this car has a carburator? i dont think i want a car with a carborator...||||reg||1
