Z||000007||MrPBody||06-25-2001||08:06 PM||||We're all prejudiced -- we love these things!<P>It's a 14-year-old car.  Its reliability depends on how well it has been cared for.  On the good side, it sounds like the current owner knows his stuff.  With any old car, you can generally expect more repairs and maintenance than a new car.  View it as an opportunity to learn.<P>I drive my '85 4-cylinder to work every day, and have driven it from Atlanta to Huntsville, Alabama, and return in one day -- about 400 miles round trip.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||Old Lar||06-25-2001||08:25 PM||||The stock side scoop is held on by 4 screws.  If you have to ask about a Fiero, I may suggest you pass.  The car is 14 years old and may need work.  They are fun to drive and not fun to fix.  If you have a reliable mechanic and the funds for the (if any) repairs, it is a different kind of car.||||reg||1
